Parts of Verified Garbage's verified assembly are adapted from other projects:
their instruction sequences, transcribed into Lean
(lean/VerifiedGarbage/Impl/, whose files say what each adapts) and emitted from
there into the crates verified-garbage-asm-<target>. This file has those
projects' notices. The targets named are the crates whose code it is in.

============================================================================
BearSSL (aarch64, arm, powerpc64le, riscv64, x86, x86_64)
============================================================================

https://www.bearssl.org/

The bitsliced AES (aes_ct, aes_ct64), its bit matrix transposition, which the
other bitsliced ciphers also use, and GHASH by integer multiplications
(ghash_ctmul32, ghash_ctmul64).

